lmlinux-ai-core (0.2.0-6) lmlinux; urgency=medium

  * Add a readiness gate to the `ai` wrapper: when the local engine
    endpoint is not answering yet but the systemd units report start-up
    in progress, wait for it with plain progress lines instead of
    letting hax's ~16 s startup auto-discovery fail ("failed to
    auto-discover model ... / is llama-server running?") and drop the
    REPL into a no-provider state — the exact first-run failure a real
    user hit on a cold live boot. A deliberately stopped or failed
    engine gets one actionable line; no curl or no systemd (chroot
    package tests) passes straight through so `ai --version` never
    blocks. Validated on the llama-server engine path; the non-default
    LiteRT-LM flavor is unchanged.

