lmlinux-ai-core (0.2.0-5) lmlinux; urgency=medium

  * Seed the hax XDG config (provider, model, llama.cpp base_url) in
    postinst: /etc/skel for accounts created later and ~/.config/hax for
    existing human users, never overwriting a present file. Bare `hax`
    in a non-login desktop shell previously had no provider/endpoint
    contract (profile.d is only sourced by login shells), so the
    interactive /provider picker probed the llama.cpp built-in default
    endpoint and reported "server not reachable" on a healthy local
    engine; the seed carries the same contract as the `ai` wrapper at
    lower precedence than environment and state.json, so interactive
    /provider and /model choices still win. The LiteRT-LM flavor keeps
    its `ai`-wrapper entry paths (hax pins hosted openai endpoints).
  * Assert both seed paths in package validation: a user created before
    the install is seeded by postinst, and a user created after it
    inherits the file from /etc/skel.

